      "q": "1. You can also make a small report comparing Abu Dhabi with the place where you live. You can use some of these points mentioned below while writing the report. You can also draw pictures or put photographs.\n(i)\nThe climate and weather\n(ii)\nWhat people wear\n(iii)\nThe trees and plants\n(iv)\nThe kind of buildings\n(v)\nThe traffic on the roads (kinds of vehicles)\n(vi)\nThe common food items\n(vii)\nThe language",
      "a": "I live in the state of Punjab in India. The differences between Punjab and Abu Dhabi according to the points given above are:\nAbu Dhabi\nPunjab\nThe climate and weather\nAs Abu Dhabi is near the sea, its climate is hot and humid throughout the year.\nPunjab is extremely hot in summers and very cold during winter.\nThe trees and plants\nOnly Date trees grow in Abu Dhabi.\nTrees such as Mango, Guava, Kinnu, etc, grow in Punjab.\nThe traffic on the roads (kinds of vehicles)\nDifferent types of cars are seen on the roads of Abu Dhabi.\nCycles, Bullock Carts, Cars and Bikes are seen on the roads of Punjab.\nThe common food items\nThe common foods in Abu Dhabi are: Harees, Salona, Madrooba and Dates\nThe common foods in Punjab are: Chhole, rice, kulcha, naan and lassi.\nWhat people wear\nThe common clothing for the people of Abu Dhabi is: Kandura, agal, bisht, burqa and hijab.\nPeople of Punjab commonly wear: Salwar suit, shirt pants and saree.\nThe kind of buildings\nVery tall buildings are present in Abu Dhabi.\nPunjab has large houses but the houses are not very tall.\nThe language\nPeople of Abu Dhabi speak Arabic and English.\nPeople of Punjab speak English, Hindi and Punjabi."
